  "worked_solution": "We model the number of cells using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=C.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nC(t)={C}_{0}\\,{e}^{t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that there are currently $650$ cells in the petri dish, so we have ${C}_{0}=650.$\n\nTherefore, the number of cells $C$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nC(t)=650\\,{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of cells when $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(2) & =650\\,{e}^{2} \\\\  & \u22484802.89\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of cells after $2$ hours is approximately $4803$ cells.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
